---
import Prose from "./Prose.astro";
// Who has bound an account to this namespace, and on what dated evidence.
//
// **Unclaimed is the ordinary state and renders as one.** Every namespace in
// this corpus is unclaimed, including all five real ones: the rows were written
// down rather than signed up for, and `author` is a free string on purpose
// because the deferred indexing lane fills it with people who never will sign
// up. So the unclaimed branch is the normal page and says so in words, the way
// every other absence here does, instead of leaving a blank where a badge goes.
//
// **This renders on the namespace's own page and nowhere else, deliberately.**
// It is not a column in the owners table, not a mark on a submission row, and
// not a line on the label view where claimants of one word sit side by side.
// The moment claimed and unclaimed appear next to each other in a list, a
// reader takes one for better, and the next reasonable step is sorting by it.
// Nothing here is sortable and no ordering anywhere derives from a claim:
// `tests/test_invariants.py` fails the build on one. See
// `schema/migrations/009` and `DECISIONS.md` 2026-09-19.
//
// **A membership is dated, never standing.** People join and leave
// organisations, so the page reports what the provider said and when it said
// it, and lets the reader decide whether that is recent enough. It never says
// an account is a member of anything now, because nothing here knows that.
interface Props {
  namespace: string;
  claims: any[];
}
const { namespace, claims } = Astro.props;

const when = (iso) =>
  new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
    year: "numeric", month: "short", day: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" });
---

{claims.length === 0 ? (
  <p class="note absent-block">
    The namespace <span class="mono">{namespace}</span> is unclaimed. Nobody has
    bound an account to it, which is the state every namespace in this registry
    is in. An author here is a free string that somebody wrote down, not an
    account somebody signed up for, and nothing about the work published under a
    namespace follows from whether anyone has claimed it.
  </p>
) : (
  claims.map((c) => (
    <div class="claim">
      <div class="provenance">
        Claimed on <time datetime={c.claimed_at}>{when(c.claimed_at)}</time> by
        the account <span class="mono">{c.provider}:{c.subject}</span>{c.handle
          ? <>, which called itself <span class="mono">{c.handle}</span> that day</>
          : <>, which gave no handle</>}
      </div>

      <p class="note">
        The claim is bound to the provider's subject id above. Handles are
        renameable on every provider here, so a claim bound to one would either
        break on a rename or follow the handle to whoever registers it next.
        {c.handle && <> The handle is recorded as of the claim date and is not
        looked up by.</>}
      </p>

      <h3>Evidence</h3>
      {c.evidence.length === 0 ? (
        <p class="note absent-block">
          No evidence was recorded with this claim, so there is nothing here to
          weigh it by.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <dl class="spec">
          {c.evidence.map((e) => (
            <>
              <dt class="mono">{e.kind}</dt>
              <dd>
                <Prose text={e.detail} />
                <div class="provenance">
                  recorded <time datetime={e.recorded_at}>{when(e.recorded_at)}</time>
                </div>
              </dd>
            </>
          ))}
        </dl>
      )}

      <h3>Organisation membership</h3>
      {c.memberships.length === 0 ? (
        <p class="note absent-block">
          Nothing has been observed about this account's organisation
          memberships. That is an absence of observation and not a statement
          that it belongs to none.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <ul class="memberships">
          {c.memberships.map((m) => (
            <li>
              Membership of <span class="mono">{m.org}</span> confirmed on{" "}
              <time datetime={m.observed_at}>{when(m.observed_at)}</time>{m.role
                ? <>, with the role <span class="mono">{m.role}</span></>
                : <>, with no role stated</>}, by{" "}
              <span class="mono">{m.source}</span>.
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )}

      <p class="note">
        Each line above is what the provider answered on that date and not a
        standing fact. People join and leave organisations, so a membership
        checked once and held forever goes stale silently. Rechecking means the
        account signs in again and a new observation is written beside this one.
      </p>
    </div>
  ))
)}

{claims.length > 1 && (
  <p class="note">
    More than one account claims this namespace. Every claim stands with its own
    evidence and this registry does not decide between them. The namespace is
    not the claim.
  </p>
)}

<p class="note">
  Claiming a namespace needs a sign-in path, and this build has none.
</p>
